Thanks, Bernd,

that is a bug and I have fixed in the svn now.

A work-around is to cast the array explicitly:

.jcall("Foo", "V", "bar2", .jcast(d, "[[I"))

(essentially the bug is that the signature of d created by .jarray is  
"[I" instead of "[[I")

Cheers,
Simon


